---The most bytes of data to return, measured once it is encoded as a JSON string. Zero or left out means 49152 (48 KiB), and values above 983040 (960 KiB) are lowered to that. Must not be negative.
---@field max_bytes? integer
---Where to start reading, in bytes from the start of the result. To read the next part, add the length in bytes of the data you received. Must not be negative.
---@field offset? integer

---@class RexComSuperlogicalTerminalBlobReadResult
---The text read, starting at offset. It never ends partway through a character. It can be shorter than max_bytes even when more text remains.
---@field data string
---True if data reaches the end of the result.
---@field eof boolean
---The result that was read. Send it in later requests so that every part comes from the same result.
---@field id integer
---The length of the whole result, in bytes.
---@field total integer

---@class RexComSuperlogicalTerminalClearArgs

---@class RexComSuperlogicalTerminalClearResult

---@class RexComSuperlogicalTerminalClipboardReadArgs
