---@field id? integer
---The most bytes of data to return, measured once it is encoded as a JSON string. Zero or left out means 49152 (48 KiB), and values above 983040 (960 KiB) are lowered to that. Must not be negative.
---@field max_bytes? integer
---Where to start reading, in bytes from the start of the text. To read the next part, add the length in bytes of the data you received. Must not be negative.
---@field offset? integer

---@class RexComSuperlogicalTerminalClipboardReadResult
---The text read, starting at offset. It never ends partway through a character. It can be shorter than max_bytes even when more text remains.
---@field data string
---True if data reaches the end of the text.
---@field eof boolean
---The copy that was read. Send it in later requests so that every part comes from the same copy.
---@field id integer
---The length of the whole copied text, in bytes.
---@field total integer

---@class RexComSuperlogicalTerminalFormatArgs
---Include the selected character sets. Only used with the vt format.
---@field extra_charsets? boolean
---Include the cursor position. Only used with the vt format.
---@field extra_cursor? boolean
---Include the hyperlink in effect at the cursor. Only used with the vt format.
---@field extra_hyperlink? boolean
---Include keyboard modes such as modifyOtherKeys. Only used with the vt format.
---@field extra_keyboard? boolean
---Include the state of the Kitty keyboard protocol. Only used with the vt format.
---@field extra_kitty_keyboard? boolean
---Include terminal modes that differ from their defaults. Only used with the vt format.
---@field extra_modes? boolean
---Include the color palette. Only used with the vt format.
---@field extra_palette? boolean
---Include the character protection mode. Only used with the vt format.
---@field extra_protection? boolean
---Include the reported working directory. Only used with the vt format.
---@field extra_pwd? boolean
---Include the scrolling region. Only used with the vt format.
---@field extra_scrolling_region? boolean
---Include the text style in effect at the cursor. Only used with the vt format.
---@field extra_style? boolean
---Include the tab stops. Only used with the vt format.
---@field extra_tabstops? boolean
---The format to return: 'text' for plain text, 'html' for HTML with inline styles, or 'vt' for escape sequences that redraw the screen with its colors and styles. Defaults to 'text'.
---@field format? string
---The most bytes of content to return, measured once it is encoded as a JSON string. If more output remains, the reply has an id, and you read the rest with blob_read. Values above 983040 (960 KiB) are lowered to that. Zero or left out returns the whole output in one reply, and the call fails with too_large if the output doesn't fit. Must not be negative.
---@field max_bytes? integer
---Remove spaces from the end of each line.
---@field trim? boolean
---Join lines that the terminal wrapped because they were too long, so each line of output is one line the program wrote.
